<TD ALIGN="left" VALIGN="top"> <P ALIGN="left" STYLE=" margin-top:0pt ; margin-bottom:0pt; font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:10pt"><B>Eaton Mobility transaction remains on track to close around the end of the first quarter of 2027</B>
</P></TD></TR></TABLE> <P STYLE="font-size:6pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt">&nbsp;</P>
<TABLE STYLE="BORDER-COLLAPSE:COLLAPSE; font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:10pt" BORDER="0" CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" WIDTH="100%">
<TR style = "page-break-inside:avoid">
<TD WIDTH="5%">&nbsp;</TD>
<TD WIDTH="3%" VALIGN="top" ALIGN="left">&#149;</TD>
<TD WIDTH="1%" VALIGN="top">&nbsp;</TD>
<TD ALIGN="left" VALIGN="top"> <P ALIGN="left" STYLE=" margin-top:0pt ; margin-bottom:0pt; font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:10pt"><B>Nearly all regulatory approvals have been obtained with only one pending</B> </P></TD></TR></TABLE>
<P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><B>MAUMEE, Ohio, October&nbsp;28, 2026 &#8211; Dana Incorporated (NYSE: DAN) today announced its third-quarter 2026 financial results, delivering strong
performance with higher sales and expanding margins. </B></P> <P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><B>&#8220;Dana delivered strong third-quarter results, reflecting our continued focus on
operating the business well and executing our strategy with discipline,&#8221; said Byron Foster, Chief Executive Officer. &#8220;Productivity gains, commercial initiatives, and structural cost reductions are driving meaningful margin improvement as
we capitalize on stronger commercial vehicle demand and continue to return capital to shareholders. As we work toward closing the Eaton Mobility transaction, we remain firmly focused on delivering strong performance today while preparing to create
an even stronger, more diversified company positioned for long-term growth and shareholder value.&#8221; </B></P> <P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><B>Sales in the third quarter of 2026
totaled $2.04&nbsp;billion, compared with $1.92&nbsp;billion in the same period of 2025. The increase was primarily driven by stronger commercial vehicle demand, backlog conversion, and commercial and cost-recovery actions. </B></P>
<P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><B>Adjusted EBITDA for the third quarter was $218&nbsp;million, representing a 10.7&nbsp;percent margin, compared with $162&nbsp;million, 8.5&nbsp;percent
margin, for the same period in 2025. Cost-savings actions, operational efficiency improvements, and commercial initiatives were the primary drivers of the improvement. </B></P>
<P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><B>Net loss from continuing operations was $10&nbsp;million in the third quarter of 2026, compared with net income of $13&nbsp;million in the same period of
2025. Diluted loss per share from continuing operations was $0.13, compared with diluted earnings per share of $0.07 last year. Significantly improved operating performance and lower net interest expense were more than offset by a $24&nbsp;million
loss on the extinguishment of debt and higher income tax expense, including a $29&nbsp;million charge related to the settlement of a foreign income tax partially offset by a $12&nbsp;million benefit associated with post <FONT
STYLE="white-space:nowrap">Off-Highway</FONT> sale restructuring actions. </B></P> <P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><B>Adjusted net income improved to $44&nbsp;million in the third quarter of
2026 from an adjusted net loss of $5&nbsp;million in the prior-year period, while diluted adjusted earnings per share improved to $0.41 from an adjusted loss per share of $0.04. </B></P>
<P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><B>Operating cash flow was $102&nbsp;million in the third quarter of 2026, compared with $111&nbsp;million in the prior-year period. Adjusted free cash flow
was $66&nbsp;million, compared with $101&nbsp;million in the prior-year period. Higher earnings from continuing operations and lower <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">one-time</FONT> costs, net interest and cash taxes partially offset the absence of
cash generation from the divested <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">Off-Highway</FONT> business, higher capital spending, and working capital timing. </B></P>
 <p STYLE="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt ; font-size:8pt">&nbsp;</P> <P STYLE="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman" ALIGN="center">1 </P>

</DIV></Center>


<p style="margin-top:1em; margin-bottom:0em; page-break-before:always"> </p>
<HR SIZE="3" style="COLOR:#999999" WIDTH="100%" ALIGN="CENTER">

<Center><DIV STYLE="width:8.5in" align="left">
 <P STYLE="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><B>Dana today announced an increase in its planned share repurchases ahead of the closing of the Eaton
Mobility transaction. During the third quarter, the company repurchased approximately 6.6&nbsp;million shares for $200&nbsp;million, bringing <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap"><FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">year-to-date</FONT></FONT> capital
returned to shareholders through share repurchases to $369&nbsp;million. Dana expects to repurchase an additional $100&nbsp;million of shares in the fourth quarter of 2026. </B></P>
<P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><B>&#8220;We continue to see compelling strategic and financial benefits from the combination with Eaton Mobility and are confident in the value the
transaction will create for our shareholders, customers, and employees,&#8221; Foster added. &#8220;As we move toward closing, we are also maximizing the opportunities available to return capital to shareholders. Our increased fourth-quarter
repurchases underscore our confidence in Dana and our commitment to shareholder value.&#8221; </B></P> <P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><B>Dana has revised its full-year guidance, raising its
sales outlook by approximately $50&nbsp;million, reflecting higher demand and recoveries. The company maintained its adjusted EBITDA, diluted adjusted EPS, and adjusted free cash flow guidance. </B></P>
<P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman"><B><U>Revised 2026 Financial Targets </U></B></P> <P STYLE="font-size:12pt;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt">&nbsp;</P>
