<img src="g160614ex99_1s24g1.jpg" alt="Slide 24" title="Slide 24" ></p> <p style="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;font-size:1pt;line-height:0pt;color:#FFFFFF;"><font style="font-family:Times New Roman;font-size:1pt;"> Eaton Mobility Transaction Update
Highly strategic combination Brings together two companies with complementary product portfolios Creates a focused, scaled powertrain leader, accelerating the Dana 2030 plan Combination to be structured as a split-off and Reverse Morris Trust
transaction Intended to be tax-free to Dana and Eaton shareholders for U.S. federal income tax purposes Provides for orderly distribution of shares to Eaton shareholders interested in New Dana Expect to achieve at least $250M run-rate cost synergies
within 24 months post-close Achievable synergy plan leveraging Dana&#8217;s strong history of cost savings realizations and successful business integrations Sales synergies expected from strong product fit and combined sales force Maintains
attractive pro forma synergized 2026 net leverage of ~1.6x, inclusive of the additional $100M in share buybacks Transaction tracking to close around the end of the first quarter of 2027 Only one remaining regulatory approval pending Mobility A
Powerful Strategic and Financial Combination, Which Provides Significant Value for Dana Shareholders Key Transaction Elements</font></p>
